stateDiagram-v2
    [*] --> PENDING: admin registers serial, secret shown once
    PENDING --> ACTIVE: first authenticated handshake
    PENDING --> EXPIRED: no handshake before device_pending_expiry_h
    ACTIVE --> STALE: unseen beyond device_unseen_alert_h, alert before lock
    STALE --> ACTIVE: authenticated heartbeat, buffered upload follows
    ACTIVE --> ROTATING: admin starts secret rotation
    ROTATING --> ACTIVE: new secret used or overlap window ends
    ACTIVE --> SUSPENDED: wrong tenant route or repeated authentication failures
    STALE --> SUSPENDED: security event
    ROTATING --> SUSPENDED: security event
    SUSPENDED --> ACTIVE: admin re-verifies and rotates the secret
    ACTIVE --> DECOMMISSIONED: admin decommissions, open erasure items routed to attestation
    STALE --> DECOMMISSIONED: admin decommissions
    SUSPENDED --> DECOMMISSIONED: admin decommissions
    DECOMMISSIONED --> SUSPENDED: same serial authenticates again, erasure items reopened
    EXPIRED --> [*]
    DECOMMISSIONED --> [*]
    note right of SUSPENDED
        Ingest refused. Delete-template and
        delete-user commands are still served,
        so erasure can finish on a returning device.
    end note
